# Quality bar (no shortcuts)

- End product = Windows agent + API + manager web. Not extension-only. Not website-only.
- Before coding a feature: read official docs for that library’s **current major version** (FastAPI / PySide6 / React / SQLAlchemy). Do not invent APIs from memory.
- One feature/module at a time. Do not start the next until the current one is **verified working** (manual test checklist in `docs/12-engineering-quality.md`).
- Prefer boring, proven patterns over novelty. No half-finished UI.
- No sugarcoating in status: say broken / blocked / done with evidence.
- Follow `07-engineering-standards.mdc`: one module fully tested before next; split large files; document behavior changes.
- Keystroke **counts only**. No stealth after Sign Out. No keylogger.
- Screenshots: random-in-interval while signed in; stop on break/sign-out (defaults in `docs/11-questions-explained-and-market-defaults.md`).
- If `STATUS.md` is not approved, docs only — no app code.
